# Advisories scripts/ci/pip_audit.sh accepts. One advisory id per line, then `#` and WHY
# it does not apply here. Every entry is a decision someone can disagree with in review;
# an entry without a reason fails the run. Prefer upgrading to adding a line here.

# python-jose: HS/RS algorithm confusion when a decode does not restrict its algorithms
# (GHSA-3qf3-8w2g-rqmx, an incomplete fix for CVE-2024-33663). No fixed release exists.
# Every jwt.decode in web_dashboard/ passes an explicit algorithm list: HS256 with the
# dashboard's own secret, or asymmetric-only (oidc_service.ASYMMETRIC_ALGS) wherever the
# key is a public JWKS. tests/test_oidc_service.py pins the OIDC case. Replacing jose with
# PyJWT removes this entry.
CVE-2026-85394  # python-jose: every decode pins its algorithms; asymmetric-only for public keys

# ecdsa: Minerva timing side channel when SIGNING with python-ecdsa (CVE-2024-23342).
# The project will not fix it. It is installed only as a python-jose dependency, and
# jose[cryptography] signs and verifies EC keys with the `cryptography` backend
# (jose.backends.ECKey is CryptographyECKey), so python-ecdsa never signs anything here.
PYSEC-2026-1325  # ecdsa: python-jose dependency only; jose uses the cryptography backend
